==English==
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|ay}} {{qualifier|New Zealand, tag question}}
* {{l|en|ehh}}, {{l|en|ehhh}}, etc. to indicate length

===Etymology 1===
Natural {{onomatopoeic|en|title=exclamation}}; first recorded mid-16th century. Perhaps an unstressed variant of {{m|en|aye|t=yes, yeah}}.
<br>The Philippine sense is possibly influenced by {{cog|tl|e}} and/or {{cog|es|eh}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{sense|tag question|request for repetition|ascertaining continued attention}}
* {{enPR|ā|a=Canada,England}}, {{IPA|en|/eɪ/}}
* {{IPA|en|/e/|a=Scotland}}
* {{audio|en|en-ca-eh.ogg|a=Canada}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪ|s=1}}
* {{hmp|en|A}}
{{sense|apathy or lack of enthusiasm|unremarkable}}
* {{enPR|ĕ|â|a=Canada,UK,US}}, {{IPA|en|/ɛ/|[ɛː]}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 eh.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Aadenboy-eh.wav|a=US|IPA=[ɛː˧˥]}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛ|s=1}}
* {{hmp|en|air<aa:one pronunciation,non-rhotic>}}

====Interjection====
{{en-intj}}

# {{lb|en|informal|chiefly|Canada|Upper Midwestern US|New Zealand|AU|UK|Irish|South Africa|India|HK|Singapore|Commonwealth}} {{n-g|Used as a [[tag question]], to emphasise what goes before or to request that the listener express an opinion about what has been said.}}
#: {{ux|en|These hot dogs are pretty good, '''eh'''?}}
#* {{Q|en|Herman Melville|Moby Dick|16|year=1851|quote=Well, what dost thou think then of seeing the world? Do ye wish to go round Cape Horn to see any more of it, '''eh'''? Can’t ye see the world where you stand?}}
# {{n-g|In isolation, a request for [[repetition]] or [[clarification]] of what has just been said.}}
#: {{syn|en|what|pardon|sorry|come again|Thesaurus:say again}}
#: {{ux|en|&mdash;I've been studying ''Graphiurus murinus''. &mdash;'''Eh'''? Studying what?}}
# {{n-g|In isolation, expressing [[surprise]] or [[confusion]].}}
#: {{syn|en|what|wha|huh|za|sorry|come again}}
#: {{ux|en|&mdash;You're going to be a dad! &mdash;'''Eh'''? You're joking!}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|chiefly|Canada}} {{n-g|An interjection used to ascertain the continued attention of someone addressed by the speaker.}}
#: {{syn|en|y'know}}
#: {{ux|en|I went to the restaurant, '''eh''', but my friends didn't show up.}}
# {{n-g|Expressing apathy or lack of enthusiasm}}; [[meh]].
#: {{ux|en|—Do you feel like going out tonight?<br/>—'''Eh''', I don't know.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|director=w:Chris Renaud; w:Pierre Coffin|title={{w|Despicable Me (film)|Despicable Me}}|year=2010|text=“Look, Mom; I made the real rocket, based on the macaroni prototype!”  “…'''Eh'''.”}}
# {{lb|en|Philippines}} {{n-g|Expressing apprehension following or preceding a [[reasoning]] or [[excuse]]}}; [[uh]].
#: {{ux|en|—Why is it like this?<br/>—'''Eh''', It's like that '''eh'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In North America, the word is stereotypically associated with [[Canada]] and can sometimes convey that the speaker is trying to sound (sarcastically) Canadian outside the country.<ref name="ca">{{cite-web |en |url=https://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/why-do-canadians-say-eh |accessdate=2025-04-01 |work={{w|Atlas Obscura}} |first=Dan |last=Nosowitz |date=2017-01-10 |title=Why Do Canadians Say ‘Eh’?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260907143326/https://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/why-do-canadians-say-eh|archivedate=7 September 2026}}</ref> However, it is in widespread use in many other parts of the English-speaking world, including the northern United States, Australia, New Zealand, England, Ireland, Malaysia, Philippines, Scotland, Wales, Singapore, South Africa, India, Hong Kong and [[Commonwealth of Nations]].

